# Security Architecture

## 1. XSS Prevention

### HTML Sanitization

MANDATORY before rendering HTML from Zulip:

```typescript
import { sanitizeHtml } from "~/shared/lib/html";
const safe = sanitizeHtml(message.content, getRealmBaseUrl());
```

- NEVER use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with raw HTML
- DOMPurify whitelist: `p, br, strong, b, em, i, a, ul, ol, li, blockquote, code, pre, span, div, img`
- Allowed attributes: `src`, `alt`
- `<script>`, `<iframe>`, `<style>`, event handlers — removed automatically

### ESLint Enforcement

```
no-eval: error
no-implied-eval: error
no-new-func: error
no-script-url: error
```

## 2. Input Validation

Use utilities from `~/shared/lib/validation`:

```typescript
import { isValidUrl, isValidRealmUrl, isValidEmail, validateFileUpload, sanitizeFilename, detectImageMime } from "~/shared/lib/validation";

if (!isValidUrl(userInput)) return;            // https: / http: only
if (!isValidRealmUrl(serverUrl)) return;       // https: with hostname only
if (!isValidEmail(email)) return;              // basic format check
const { valid, error } = validateFileUpload(file);  // size, non-empty
const safeName = sanitizeFilename(file.name);   // strips <>:"/\|?* and path traversal
const mime = detectImageMime(buffer);           // magic bytes, not extension
```

## 3. Auth & Credentials

| Data | Storage | Transmission |
|------|---------|--------------|
| API Key | `localStorage` (plain JSON) | ONLY `Authorization: Basic` header |
| Password | NEVER stored | POST to /fetch_api_key only |
| Realm URL | `localStorage` | Open |
| Theme/UI | `localStorage` | — |

### Auth Header Construction

Single point: `buildAuthHeader()` from `~/shared/lib/auth-guard`:

```typescript
import { buildAuthHeader } from "~/shared/lib/auth-guard";
const headers = buildAuthHeader();  // { Authorization: "Basic ..." } or {}
```

DO NOT construct auth headers manually in new code. The middleware client (`shared/api/client.ts`) uses `authMiddleware` which calls `buildAuthHeader`.

### Secure Logout

```typescript
import { wipeCredentials } from "~/shared/lib/auth-guard";
wipeCredentials();  // Clears localStorage + Zustand store
```

### Session Timeout

`initAuthGuard()` — auto-logout after 24h of inactivity.
Activity tracking: mousemove, keydown, click, scroll, touch.

### Known Risk: localStorage + XSS

API Key is stored in localStorage as plain text. If an XSS attack executes JS code, it can read the apiKey. Mitigation:
- **CSP** blocks script injection
- **DOMPurify** sanitizes all HTML from Zulip
- **ESLint** forbids eval/new Function/script URL
- **Session timeout** limits session lifetime
- **Sentry/Logger** redact credentials

Full localStorage encryption provides no protection against XSS (JS that can read localStorage can also decrypt it).

### Rules

- API Key NEVER in URL query params
- API Key NEVER in logs
- On logout → `wipeCredentials()` (not manual cleanup)
- `JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(...))` — always in `try/catch`
- New code: use `buildAuthHeader()`, don't construct manually

## 4. Content Security Policy

### Electron (main.ts — already implemented)

Prod CSP:
```
default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline';
connect-src 'self' https: wss:; img-src 'self' data: https:;
font-src 'self'; media-src 'self' https:; frame-src https:
```

### Web (index.html)

Security meta tags:
```html
<meta http-equiv="X-Content-Type-Options" content="nosniff" />
<meta name="referrer" content="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" />
```

Vite dev/preview server adds:
- `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`
- `Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin`
- `Permissions-Policy: camera=self, microphone=self, fullscreen=self, geolocation=()`
- Preview: `X-Frame-Options: DENY`

### Production web server (nginx/CDN)

Add to configuration:
```
X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
X-Frame-Options: DENY
Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
Permissions-Policy: camera=self, microphone=self, fullscreen=self, geolocation=()
Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; ...
```

## 5. Electron Security

### Required Settings (already in main.ts)

```typescript
webPreferences: {
  contextIsolation: true,     // REQUIRED — isolates preload from renderer
  nodeIntegration: false,     // REQUIRED — no Node.js in renderer
  sandbox: true,              // REQUIRED — restricts renderer privileges
}
```

### Navigation Guard (already implemented)

```typescript
mainWindow.webContents.on("will-navigate", (event, url) => {
  if (!url.startsWith(appOrigin)) {
    event.preventDefault();         // block navigation
    if (isSafeExternalUrl(url)) {
      shell.openExternal(url);      // open in system browser
    }
  }
});
```

### URL Validation for shell.openExternal

```typescript
function isSafeExternalUrl(url: string): boolean {
  const parsed = new URL(url);
  return parsed.protocol === "https:" || parsed.protocol === "http:" || parsed.protocol === "mailto:";
}
```

Blocked: `javascript:`, `file:`, `data:`, `ftp:`, `vbscript:`, custom protocols.

### IPC

- Expose ONLY a minimal API via `contextBridge`
- Every IPC handler — validate input data
- Don't pass filesystem paths through IPC

## 6. Sensitive Data in Logs

Logger (`~/shared/lib/logger`) automatically redacts:
- **Keys**: apiKey, password, token, authorization, secret, csrf, session, cookie
- **Values**: `Basic ...`, `Bearer ...`, long base64 strings

Rules:
- DO NOT log HTTP request/response bodies (PII)
- DO NOT log message content
- DO NOT display stack traces to the user in production
- Use `logger` instead of `console.log` (ESLint `no-console`)

## 7. Dependencies

- `npm audit --audit-level=high` — fail CI on critical/high
- Dependabot (`.github/dependabot.yml`) — weekly npm check, monthly for GH Actions
- `save-exact=true` in `.npmrc` — pin versions
- DOMPurify — update with priority (critical for XSS)

## 8. Deep Link / IPC Input Validation

### Deep Links

All incoming deep link routes are validated by `isSafeDeeplinkRoute()` in `main.ts`:
- Rejects `javascript:`, `data:`, `vbscript:` protocols
- Rejects URLs containing `//` (prevents protocol-relative injection)
- Enforces max length (512 chars)
- Applied in `handleDeepLink()` and `pendingDeepLink` delivery

### IPC Input Validation (Electron main.ts)

Every IPC handler validates its input:

| Channel | Validation |
|---------|-----------|
| `theme:set` | Only accepts `"light"`, `"dark"`, `"system"` |
| `notifications:show` | Title/body type-checked + truncated to 200 chars |
| `os:setBadgeCount` | Non-negative integer, clamped |
| `os:setProgressBar` | Float 0-1 or -1 (reset) |
| `os:setLoginItemSettings` | Boolean only |
| `call:start` | Room string sanitized (control chars removed, max 128) |

### WebView Bridge

Auth tokens passed via `postMessage` bridge only — NEVER in URL params.
`handleIncomingMessage()` checks `event.data.type` is a known value.

## 9. Push Notification Security

- FCM tokens are NEVER logged (token prefix only: `abc123...`)
- Push payload goes through middleware pipeline: decrypt → parse → validate → dedup
- Encrypted payloads that cannot be decrypted are dropped (not displayed)
- Notification display text is truncated (no full message body in system notifications)
- Push token is unregistered on logout via `unregisterPushToken()`

## 10. Analytics & Monitoring Privacy

- PII keys auto-stripped before sending: `email`, `password`, `token`, `phone`, `ssn`, `creditcard`
- Message content NEVER sent to analytics
- User ID sent as numeric ID only (not email)
- Consent required before any analytics data is sent
- Sentry: `beforeSend` strips auth headers, cookies, and PII from error reports

## 11. Secure Coding Principles

These principles are enforced at compile time, lint time, pre-commit, and runtime:

| Principle | Enforcement |
|-----------|-------------|
| No raw HTML rendering | Pre-commit hook blocks `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without `sanitizeHtml` |
| No code execution from strings | ESLint: `no-eval`, `no-implied-eval`, `no-new-func`, `no-script-url` |
| No hardcoded secrets | Pre-commit secret detection + `.gitignore` for `.env`, `.pem`, `.key` |
| Input validation at boundaries | `guard.*` functions + `invariant()` + `isValidUrl()` |
| Minimal IPC surface | `contextBridge` exposes only documented methods |
| Credential redaction in logs | Logger auto-redacts 15 sensitive key patterns |
| Defense in depth | CSP + DOMPurify + ESLint + Pre-commit + Runtime guards |

## 12. Security Review Checklist

### For every PR:

- [ ] No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without `sanitizeHtml()`
- [ ] URLs from user input validated with `isValidUrl()` or `guard.url()`
- [ ] Files validated via `validateFileUpload()` + `detectImageMime()`
- [ ] No credentials in logs, comments, error messages, URLs
- [ ] No `eval()`, `new Function()`, `document.write()`
- [ ] IPC handlers validate and sanitize all input
- [ ] External URLs opened via `isSafeExternalUrl()` → `shell.openExternal()`
- [ ] `localStorage` access wrapped in `try/catch`
- [ ] New env vars are NOT secrets (Vite exposes `VITE_*` to client)
- [ ] `JSON.parse()` on external data wrapped in `try/catch`
- [ ] Push tokens not logged (only prefix)
- [ ] Deep link routes validated before navigation
- [ ] Role checks (`hasPermission()`) for admin-only actions
- [ ] No `Math.random()` for security-sensitive values (use `crypto.randomUUID()`)
